sequenceDiagram
    participant App as App<br>[implements GapPeripheralResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapPeripheral]
    participant Central as BLE Central


    Note over Node, Central: Messages between Node and BLE Central<br>are link-layer events, not driven by the App.<br>The App only observes them through<br>Echo callbacks (e.g. CurrentState).

    App->>Node: GapPeripheral.SetAllowPairing(false)
    App->>Node: GapPeripheral.Advertise(type=advInd, advertisingInterval=160)
    Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(advertising)

    Note over App, Central: With SetAllowPairing(false), non-bonded peers cannot connect at all.<br>Only already-bonded centrals may reconnect<br>(and re-encrypt using the stored keys).

    alt Connecting central has no bond
        alt Peripheral rejects at LL (advertisement filtering)
            Central-)Node: CONNECT_IND
            Note over App, Central: Peripheral never accepts CONNECT_IND.<br>No LL connection is established.
            Note over App: No CurrentState callback fires.<br>Node continues advertising.
        else Peripheral accepts LL, then disconnects at higher layer
            Central-)Node: CONNECT_IND
            Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(connected)
            rect rgb(245, 230, 230)
                Node-)Central: LL_TERMINATE_IND
            end
            Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
            Note over App: App observes a brief connected transition,<br>then standby. App may call Advertise() again.
        end
        Note over App, Central: Which of these two paths occurs is stack-dependent.
    else Connecting central is already bonded
        Central-)Node: CONNECT_IND
        Node-->>App: GapPeripheralResponse.CurrentState(connected)
        rect rgb(245, 240, 230)
            Note over Node, Central: LL encryption using the stored LTK (no SMP)
            Central-)Node: LL_ENC_REQ (Rand, EDIV, SKD_M, IV_M)
            Node-)Central: LL_ENC_RSP (SKD_S, IV_S)
            Node-)Central: LL_START_ENC_REQ (encrypted)
            Central-)Node: LL_START_ENC_RSP (encrypted)
            Node-)Central: LL_START_ENC_RSP (encrypted)
        end
        Note over App: Link re-encrypted using existing bond keys.<br>No new SMP procedure and no AuthenticationRequired.
    end
